data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":2345,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0987dc3a8b1d630d016ad368f64ae08191a85633318b0b06b1","object":"response","created_at":1792239862,"completed_at":1792239926,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6-astra","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"GPT-6 Astra design-only review request\n\nThis request is limited to the exact SPEC-071 design packet below. Review the packet bytes with SHA-256 439bab94579ad33c174afde2612031c9d0f1afbc593ebb903524c38ec1e246b7 (149350 bytes). Do not infer that unprovided files or omitted Dashboard content were reviewed.\n\nRequested outcome: return exactly one top-level verdict: APPROVE (design readiness only), AMEND, or NO-GO. State explicitly: implementation authorization: NO.\n\nAssess only whether SPEC-071 v0.12-draft is coherent, sufficiently bounded, testable, privacy-safe, and suitable to proceed to final SPEC review. The tool has not been implemented. Do not claim code, test, runtime, or output validation. Give numbered findings with exact supplied file/section references. Separate must-fix design blockers from optional hardening. Preserve the owner’s decisions and authority; do not modify files or authorize implementation.\n\nConsider the five NG-070 drift cases and the selected controls. Identify missing acceptance criteria, false-clean/false-progress risks, unresolved schema/CLI contract issues, packet-evidence limitations, and any contradiction in the use of Hermes decision_query. If evidence is insufficient, say so and bound the verdict rather than infer.\n","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0987dc3a8b1d630d016ad368f989208191bb25249eaa0f415e","summary":[],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq02j5VKjslt0Us66vTLHgHicDXOFtz3TZ9iM-9-4l4hE6RTXepIy6GTiDyEUG59Kj0Vh8wlfeE3LgnUaTiDsBlh0pQNm9ocLlLXP8-Jf4lJe8JrWTCe943XJdnWobD59_K1BkvG6fiiE3